[["page","lines",16],{"text":"additional data from the managing structure, allowing us to compare the organized screening rate","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":294.8759,"width":470.27057370999967,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",17],{"text":"during our experiment with that found several months before and after our experiment. These","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":316.7989,"width":470.2683918899995,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",18],{"text":"organized screening rates appear in Table V in Appendix D. We have no information on opportunistic","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":338.72090000000003,"width":470.2738464399996,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",19],{"text":"screening for other time periods. Assuming that opportunistic screening is fairly stable over time,","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":360.64390000000003,"width":470.2727555299996,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",20],{"text":"the comparison of the take-up rates in the organized program provides support for the Type-I error","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":382.56590000000006,"width":470.26839188999975,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",21],{"text":"interpretation. The newly eligible in our experiment have an uptake rate of 60%, including 53.8%","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":404.48890000000006,"width":470.2738464399995,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",22],{"text":"who screen within the program. In sharp contrast, the comparable figure for other time periods","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":426.4109000000001,"width":470.26948279999976,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",23],{"text":"is never over 50.9%, with an average of 46.9%, supporting the view that we observed abnormally","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":448.3339000000001,"width":470.26621006999994,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",24],{"text":"high rates in our experiment. In addition, the screening-rate difference between the control and","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":470.2559000000001,"width":470.2694827999999,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",25],{"text":"treatment groups in the Eure does not attain the usual significance benchmarks when controlling for","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":492.1789000000001,"width":470.26730097999973,"height":10.909100000000024}]
[["page","lines",26],{"text":"multiple hypothesis testing. A third possibility is that treatments did have a real depressing effect","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":514.1009000000001,"width":470.2727555299996,"height":10.90910000000008}]
[["page","lines",27],{"text":"on newly-eligible women in the Eure. We cannot rule out this possibility.","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":536.0239000000001,"width":347.4701077399998,"height":10.90910000000008}]
[["page","lines",28],{"text":"Overall, the negative differences for the newly eligible are driven by the Eure and especially by","fontSize":10.9091,"x":87.80300000000001,"y":557.9469000000001,"width":453.33528686999966,"height":10.90910000000008}]
[["page","lines",29],{"text":"the surprisingly high screening rate in the control group. We should be cautious in interpreting this","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":579.8689000000002,"width":470.2727555299997,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",30],{"text":"as a negative effect of our behavioral interventions on the newly eligible.","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":601.7919000000002,"width":343.65519546999997,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",31],{"text":"What do we then learn from the newly eligible? We believed that treatment effects would be","fontSize":10.9091,"x":87.80300000000001,"y":623.7139000000002,"width":453.3276505,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",32],{"text":"more likely in a group that had a greater chance of reading the invitation letters. For instance,","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":645.6369000000002,"width":470.27166461999934,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",33],{"text":"if learning occurs through trial and error, these women may change the information they consider","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":667.5589000000002,"width":470.2662100699995,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",34],{"text":"to be relevant and thus their behavior. However, our analysis provides suggestive evidence that","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.86600000000001,"y":689.4819000000002,"width":470.26402825,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",35],{"text":"17","fontSize":10.9091,"x":300.576,"y":740.1129000000002,"width":10.848009040000022,"height":10.909099999999967}]
